Lab 13: Configuring Cross-Forest Trust with Active Directory
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the concept of cross-forest trust between Identity Management (IdM) and Active Directory
Configure a cross-forest trust using the ipa trust-add command
Map POSIX attributes to Active Directory users for seamless integration
Verify and test access to Active Directory resources from IdM-managed systems
Troubleshoot common trust relationship issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with Active Directory concepts and terminology
Knowledge of DNS configuration and name resolution
Understanding of Kerberos authentication principles
Experience with command-line interface operations
Completed previous IdM labs or equivalent knowledge
Required Knowledge Areas
Active Directory Domain Services: Understanding of AD domains, forests, and trust relationships
Identity Management (IdM): Basic IdM server configuration and management
DNS Configuration: Forward and reverse DNS zone management
Kerberos: Authentication protocols and ticket-granting concepts
LDAP: Directory service protocols and attribute mapping
